    },
    {
      "text": "The new documentation clarifies the company's revenue model by stating, \"We make most of our money from private search ads on our search engine,\" and emphasizes that these ads are targeted to your current search results rather than built from a personal profile. This reassures users that advertising does not require tracking their behavior across the web.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "hunk": "h1",
          "side": "added",
          "quote": "We make most of our money from private search ads on our search engine."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Readers should note that while the default experience remains completely anonymous, enabling optional tools like Email Protection or Sync & Backup means the company will handle limited personal data, as the policy now states, \"For optional features, we only request personal information necessary for the feature to function and only use the information for that purpose.\" This change requires users to actively opt into these services and review their specific privacy terms.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "hunk": "h1",
          "side": "added",
          "quote": "For optional features, we only request personal information necessary for the feature to function and only use the information for that purpose."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The updated policy modernizes its legal stance by acknowledging potential cross-border data transfers and formal user rights, while firmly maintaining that, \"Critically, it's not possible for us to provide search, chat, or browsing histories linked to you in response to legal requests because we don't have them.\" This sets clearer expectations for how limited contact information might be handled during legal inquiries compared to the older version's hypothetical leak examples.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "hunk": "h1",
          "side": "added",
          "quote": "Critically, it's not possible for us to provide search, chat, or browsing histories linked to you in response to legal requests because we don't have them."
        }
