    {
      "text": "The documentation streamlines its technical explanations by directly asserting, \"We don’t track you through cookies or any other storage methods,\" and clarifying that any browser storage used is strictly anonymous and reserved for display preferences or experimental testing. This removes older debates about HTTP referrers and POST requests, focusing instead on the practical outcome: no persistent tracking identifiers.",
